  "description": "BAGVUD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H102 N8 Ni3 O41 Tb4,C4 H10 O1,1.5(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.283-4.438 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.23-133.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H102N8Ni3O41Tb4·Et2O·1.5MeOH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
